/-!
# Scalar constituents of the genuine larger-field local residual

For |F| = 2^n, n > 1, the full point parabolic P equals O²(P). Its literal
block quotient is GL₂(F), with scalar character χ = det⁻¹. The natural
flag has actions χ and B; the dual flag has B⁻ᵀ and χ⁻¹; the actual
unipotent radical has action χ B⁻ᵀ. All five actions are irreducible among
arbitrary additive subgroups and are noncentral. The scalar constituents
have order 2^n and the plane constituents have order 2^(2n). Concrete
alternating-form intertwiners identify the plane restrictions to SL₂(F).

The full parabolic core is the block kernel. Quotient maps and the
proved determinant-one alignment transport the actions to the original
L₁, including its literal radical section, V₁, V/V₁ and every marked
upper/lower copy. The original terminal quotient L₁/O₂(L₁) is GL₂(F)
and has no nontrivial ambient-normal two-section or two-chief factor.

In the source flags, the additional noncentral scalar occurrences are
V₁ itself, the scalar line in each of the r upper natural copies, and
the scalar quotient in each of the s lower dual copies. Their binary
isomorphism types need not be distinct. The prior MarkedLayers premises
remain explicit. The intersection calculation and final G.2.5(8) chief
count remain with the parent assembly; neither is asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
Hypothesis G.2.1 and G.2.5(8), printed pp.332,335–336.
-/
